+REPORT 10r2 — Status DONE
+
+Changes
+- docs/measurement/ttfv-protocol.md
+  - (1) q3 key (b) now reads: "shown not to be worse than the baseline by more than the allowed drop (`delta`), i.e. non-inferior within `delta` (the lower bound on the candidate-minus-baseline difference is above `-delta`)". Scoring note 5.2 gains: an answer to q3 (or a PASS interpretation) that says only "not shown to be worse" describes INCONCLUSIVE too and is scored incorrect. The PASS branch of 5.3 ("**PASS** meets q3's key") was left unchanged; it now inherits the non-inferiority wording and reads correctly.
+  - (2) Single run-store definition in 4.2: "The run store, written `<store>` below, is `runs/<experiment_id>/` unless `--out` names another directory." 4.3 (`ls/shasum/arci gate <store>`), 4.5 (`<store>/trials.jsonl`) and 4.6 ("`trials.jsonl` in the run store (4.2)") use it; no other `runs/` path remains.
+  - (3) Precondition 2.3: after a wheel attempt the facilitator checks the installed version equals `package.version` (`uv tool list` is enough) and records any mismatch in `failures`.
+  - (4) 4.6: for an attempt with no valid verdict, `descriptor_hand_edited` is true if the reader edited `arci.yaml` by hand before any `arci run` that started trials.
+  - (5) One-line chain rule: `descriptor_written` at the first output of `arci run`; `run_start` there too only if that invocation printed a valid verdict; otherwise follow 4.1 and stamp it at the later `arci run` that does.
+- docs/measurement/receipt.template.json
+  - durations and outcome `_comment`s: `runs/<id>` replaced by "trials.jsonl in the run store (protocol 4.2)".
